---
description: People Strategy Intelligence product and design rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Before implementing any UI, determine which workflow stage the screen supports: Strategy, Measurement, Data, Analysis, or Action.

The UI must prioritize the business decision and evidence over decoration.

Public pages are single-column case studies plus Architecture / Perspective / About. Do not revive a three-column workbench unless the owner reopens a file-analysis product.

Do not introduce new colors, radii, font sizes, shadows, or visual patterns outside the design system without an explicit reason.

Do not build generic dashboard pages. Every analytical view must have a clear business question, takeaway headline, evidence, and next action.

AI recommendations must visibly distinguish proposals, assumptions, approved definitions, and missing evidence.

The early file-analysis experiment (`/lab`, `/workbench`, Formulator `/app`) is retired. Do not add file-upload surfaces on the public site.

All People data objects start with `people` (`people_mart_*`, `people_workspaces`, lake folders `people_bronze` / `people_silver` / `people_gold`). See `.cursor/rules/people-naming.mdc`.
